\in Z,\\,{n}^{2}=25$"} :step/id #uuid "5cc4daae-92a4-562a-b0bc-69db33a25a95" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414824}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414823 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414818 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21397aad-294d-5cb0-8fc2-55534f4a6fba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "∃\\,n\\in N,\\,∀\\,x\\in R,\\,x+n>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414789} {:answer/id #uuid "4ec06de9-0d99-57b0-9a3a-16fc00cab7e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "∀\\,x\\in R,\\,∃\\,n\\in N,\\,x+n>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414796} {:answer/id #uuid "75fd620c-3826-539d-aadf-0db05cc1c187" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "∃\\,x\\in R,\\,∀\\,n\\in N,\\,x+n>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414801} {:answer/id #uuid "884a72c8-4262-5b6c-97e1-72f59632519a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "∃\\,x\\in R,\\,∀\\,n\\in N,\\,xn>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414806} {:answer/id #uuid "9effbd25-3f4e-52ec-adfe-e05327867b1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "∀\\,n\\in N,\\,∃\\,x\\in R,\\,x+n>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414808}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414801} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9937ecd-67a0-55f8-9d21-e9472a02b1f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414815}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "61ea11f5-e114-5b4e-93aa-fef7b636de63" :question/math-academy-id "q-183569" :question/problem "There is a real number such that, added to any natural number, gives a positive number.\n\nExpress the above in formal language." :question/worked-solution "Notice that our sentence can be re-phrased as \n\nThere exists a real number $x$ such that, added to any natural number, gives a positive number.\n\nNow, \"$x$ added to any natural number gives a positive number\" means that\n\nFor any natural number $n,$ we have that $x+n>0.$\n\nTherefore, we get the following statement:\n\nThere exists a real number $x$ such that for any natural number $n$ we have that $x+n>0.$\n\nMore formally, this reads as\n\n$∃\\,x\\in R,\\,∀\\,n\\in N,\\,x+n>0.$"} :step/id #uuid "684e8d56-c781-5037-9fa3-b779df0822ad" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414825}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414824 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414820 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36385d37-b616-5435-802e-28750f745704" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "∃\\,k\\in Z,\\,{k}^{2}=512" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414793} {:answer/id #uuid "43a6f437-2d46-5135-bb5c-65973d31af6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "∀\\,k\\in Z,\\,{2}^{k}=512" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414795} {:answer/id #uuid "6ba09872-e3ca-54c9-806a-1e8cf5a8c8b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "∃\\,k\\in Z,\\,{2}^{k}=512" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414800} {:answer/id #uuid "927875d6-c6c6-5ddb-a6ea-953be6ea498a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "∀\\,k\\in Z,\\,k=\\sqrt{512}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414807} {:answer/id #uuid "d95df757-4f9e-5360-a232-168c68f04785" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "∃\\,k\\in Z,\\,k={512}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414811}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414800} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5da8752-1f0d-59e0-a94c-e374bf67e5d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414817}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8f1922dc-ffa7-525a-929e-f25f8887b492" :question/math-academy-id "q-183556" :question/problem "$512$ is a power of base $2.$\n\nExpress the statement above in formal language." :question/worked-solution "Recall that \"$512$ is a power of base $2$\" means the following:\n\nThere exists an integer $k$ such that ${2}^{k}=512.$\n\nMore formally, this reads as follows:\n\n$∃\\,k\\in Z,\\,{2}^{k}=512$"} :step/id #uuid "7d4c67a0-d61f-5e10-ac71-f09f134d7a7a" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414823}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414825 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414821 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14428b06-3047-50b9-aa88-3ad9212e487b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "∀\\,k\\in Z,\\,∃\\,q\\in Q,\\,kq=k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414788} {:answer/id #uuid "337eee28-d0ff-5774-974d-6f7b31464bc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "∃\\,k\\in Z,\\,∃\\,q\\in Q,\\,kq=q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414792} {:answer/id #uuid "7bad8008-4b08-5444-bc02-a16600d66a30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "∀\\,q\\in Q,\\,∃\\,k\\in Z,\\,kq=q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414802} {:answer/id #uuid "84a0f7dc-748f-5977-98f4-cc7c7bcb7a32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "∃\\,k\\in Z,\\,∀\\,q\\in Q,\\,kq=q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414803} {:answer/id #uuid "c314ce38-5463-5799-a600-f517694af5db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "∃\\,q\\in Q,\\,∀\\,k\\in Z,\\,kq=k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414809}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414803} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd95aa99-f4e5-52d5-a54e-5119eca0a5a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414816}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f4dd7341-6f18-5e73-afaa-e4cf5a0832e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-183715" :question/problem "There exists an integer number such that, for any rational number, the product of both numbers is the second number.\n\nExpress the statement above in formal language." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our statement:\n\n- The words \"there exists\" indicate that we use an existential quantifier, $∃.$\n\n- The word \"any\" indicates that we use a universal quantifier, $∀.$\n\n- The sentence refers to integers and rational numbers. So, by denoting our numbers as $k$ and $q,$ respectively, we have\n\n$$\n∃\\,k\\in Z,\\,∀\\,q\\in Q.\n$$\n\n- Finally, the condition in the statement can be written as follows:\n\n$$\nkq=q\n$$\n\nTherefore, we write the statement as follows:\n\n$∃\\,k\\in Z,\\,∀\\,q\\in Q,\\,kq=q$"} :step/id #uuid "d0fd9634-715c-5f74-8009-1d3e9fd3b761" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414826}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414826 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414819 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60f48153-5303-511e-a5c1-204d5bb84306" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "∀\\,x\\in R,\\,∃\\,k\\in Z,\\,{x}^{k}\\in Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414798} {:answer/id #uuid "665dd058-0658-5bbd-a0ab-dcb1fc441209" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "∃\\,x\\in R,\\,∃\\,k\\in Z,\\,{x}^{k}\\in Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414799} {:answer/id #uuid "857fcb90-58e7-5169-a4e8-cdffb26d856a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "∃\\,k\\in Z,\\,∀\\,x\\in R,\\,{x}^{k}\\in Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414804} {:answer/id #uuid "87bd3680-2669-50c3-a706-c4f21ca5a8f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "∀\\,k\\in Z,\\,∃\\,x\\in R,\\,{x}^{k}\\in Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414805} {:answer/id #uuid "cfdf3270-1913-5243-b0a3-4b9066c9a5ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "∃\\,x\\in R,\\,∀\\,k\\in Z,\\,{x}^{k}\\in Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414810}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414810} :answer-field/id #uuid "3cdc6710-ca1a-5981-b0a2-0186ffd3f509" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414813}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "822441e0-0d3a-577b-9cb1-929e6c39db8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-183717" :question/problem "There is a real number such that, raised to any integer, the result is a rational number.\n\nExpress the statement above in formal language." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our statement:\n\n- The words \"there exists\" indicate that we use an existential quantifier, $∃.$\n\n- The word \"any\" indicates that we use a universal quantifier, $∀.$\n\n- The sentence refers to real numbers and integers. So, by denoting our numbers as $x$ and $k,$ respectively, we have\n\n$$\n∃\\,x\\in R,\\,∀\\,k\\in Z.\n$$\n\n- Finally, the condition in the statement can be written as follows:\n\n$$\n{x}^{k}\\in Q\n$$\n\nTherefore, we write the statement as follows:\n\n$∃\\,x\\in R,\\,∀\\,k\\in Z,\\,{x}^{k}\\in Q$"} :step/id #uuid "dfab1f2b-4555-5bd9-9f40-20d004a7cae8"}] :activity/title "Formal and Informal Language" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414787}]}
